   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of the\nstate highway system as the \"Patrolman David 'DW' Smith Memorial Highway\"",
    "basePrintNo": "S8609",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8609-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §344-n, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8609\n\nSPONSOR: AKSHAR\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of\nthe state highway system as the \"Patrolman David 'DW' Smith Memorial\nHighway\"\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill renames a section of New York State Route 17C within the\nVillage of Johnson City the \"Patrolman David 'DW' Smith Memorial High-\nway.\"\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: of the bill adds section 344-n to the highway law to desig-\nnate a portion of New York State Route 17C in the Village of Johnson\nCity as the \"Patrolman David 'DW' Smith Memorial Highway.\"\n\nSection 2: Provides for the installation and maintenance of signage to\nbe undertaken by the New York State Department of Transportation.\n\nSection 3: States the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn 2014, Police Officer David 'DW' Smith was shot and killed after\nresponding to a disturbance call at business in Johnson City. Officer\nSmith served with the Johnson City Police Department for 18-1/2 years.\nIn honor of his service and sacrifice, the Village of Johnson City has\nrequested to rename a portion of 17C the \"Patrolman David 'DW' Smith\nMemorial Highway.\"\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPACT:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
